    <sys:String x:Key="Ai_HelpTitle" xml:space="preserve">How to connect AI — guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Ai_HelpSteps" xml:space="preserve">1. Pick a provider: Mock — offline demo, no key; OpenAI-compatible — OpenAI, OpenRouter, or local Ollama / LM Studio (in development, may have issues); Anthropic — Claude (in development, may have issues); Gemini — Google.
2. The API base URL and model are filled in automatically — change them manually if needed. Enter only the bare base address (e.g. https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com), without /v1beta/models/… .
3. Paste the API key. Where to get it: OpenAI — platform.openai.com/api-keys; Anthropic — console.anthropic.com; Gemini — aistudio.google.com/apikey (free). No key is needed for Ollama / LM Studio.
4. Click “Test connection” — you should see “Connection OK (reply: OK)”.
5. Click “Save”. The key is stored encrypted on this PC and is sent nowhere except the selected provider.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Ai_Privacy" xml:space="preserve">Note: an external provider (not Mock) receives lecture and test texts and student answers — without names. Do not use it for confidential material without your institution's approval.</sys:String>
